{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"PR #652 CI showed container-smoke failing with Connection refused immediately after mosquitto -d and runner-smoke failing before gnostic-runner reported online; the same checks passed locally, indicating both tests raced asynchronous broker startup.","decision":"Before testing the broker or launching gnostic-runner, retry a non-retained mosquitto_pub readiness probe for up to five seconds and fail with a specific broker readiness message on timeout.","impact":"Updated only Scripts/container-smoke.sh and Scripts/runner-smoke.sh. No application behavior or dependency changed. The original PR CI failures occurred before this fix; container execution is blocked locally by the existing build mount permissions, while shell syntax and harness-test pass.","recurrence_control":"The two smoke commands now verify an actual broker connection rather than relying on daemon startup timing. bash -n, make harness-test, and git diff --check passed.","rejected_alternatives":["Add a fixed sleep that does not prove the broker is accepting connections.","Change Runtime or runner startup behavior when the CI log identifies broker readiness as the failure boundary."],"sources":[]}
